 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for committed changes.** Fast updates without a realtime provider dependency or recurring realtime-service fees justify owning connection capacity, publication, and reconnect operations. Five-second HTTPS polling would simplify stateless operations but add repeated reads and seconds of lag; a hosted realtime service would reduce connection operations but introduce recurring fees and provider coupling. See [Delivery of Board Changes](decisions/change-delivery.md).
